+    Found on pilot 052001's frames (owner, 2026-09-27):
+    - After a death the game spectates a teammate, whose HUD reads present with an hp of its own (max 275 there) for
+      the ~7 s until respawn. So a death runs from an hp-0 sample to the first later sample that reads Spider-Man's own
+      HUD again: his web-charge counter (`webs`) and a positive hp. A team holds one Spider-Man, so a spectated teammate
+      never shows the counter.
+    - A post-match scene reads a bright health-bar strip with no hp. So present needs a read hp (reader misses shorter
+      than hi.MAX_HUD_GAP_NS stay inside gameplay, as in range mode).
+    - After a HUD absence longer than HUD_HOLE_NS, samples within HUD_RETURN_SETTLE_NS of the HUD's return read
+      absent (False): the round-start splash.
+    True/False/None are kept as read otherwise, as in range mode."""
+    hud = [(r["composition_ns"], r["hud_present"] if r["hud_present"] is not True else r.get("hp") is not None)
+           for r in samples]
+    settled, last_present, absent_since, resume = [], None, None, None
+    for t, p in hud:
+        if p is True:
+            if absent_since is not None and t - absent_since > HUD_HOLE_NS:
+                resume = t + HUD_RETURN_SETTLE_NS
+            absent_since = None
+            settled.append((t, False if resume is not None and t < resume else True))
